---
title: Code Mode with Snippets
id: code-mode-with-snippets
order: 3
description: "Teach Code Mode to save and reuse working code as named snippets backed by persistent storage — faster follow-up requests and composable agent memory."
keywords:
  - tanstack ai
  - code mode
  - snippets
  - snippet library
  - register_snippet
  - reusable snippets
  - agent memory
  - snippet storage
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Snippets extend "},{"type":"link","href":"./code-mode.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Code Mode"}]},{"type":"text","value":" with a persistent library of reusable TypeScript snippets. When the LLM writes a useful piece of code — say, a function that fetches and ranks NPM packages — it can save that code as a "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"snippet"}]},{"type":"text","value":". On future requests, relevant snippets are loaded from storage and made available as first-class tools the LLM can call without re-writing the logic."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Different from agent-authoring skills."}]},{"type":"text","value":" The snippets on this page are "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"runtime"}]},{"type":"text","value":" snippets the chat LLM saves and reuses. If you're looking to teach your coding assistant (Claude Code, Cursor, etc.) how TanStack AI itself works, see "},{"type":"link","href":"../getting-started/agent-skills","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Agent Skills (TanStack Intent)"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"overview","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Overview"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The snippets system has two integration paths:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Approach"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Entry point"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Snippet selection"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Best for"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"High-level"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"codeModeWithSnippets()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Automatic (LLM-based)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"New projects, turnkey setup"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Manual"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Individual functions ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"snippetsToTools"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createSnippetManagementTools"},{"type":"text","value":", etc.)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You decide which snippets to load"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Full control, existing setups"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Both paths share the same storage, trust, and execution primitives — they differ only in how snippets are selected and assembled."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"how-it-works","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How It Works"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A request with snippets enabled goes through these stages:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ 1. Load snippet index (metadata only, no code)        │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 2. Select relevant snippets (LLM call — fast model)   │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 3. Build tool registry                              │\n│    ├── execute_typescript (Code Mode sandbox)        │\n│    ├── search_snippets / get_snippet / register_snippet   │\n│    └── snippet tools (one per selected snippet)         │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 4. Generate system prompt                           │\n│    ├── Code Mode type stubs                         │\n│    └── Snippet library documentation                  │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 5. Main chat() call (strong model)                  │\n│    ├── Can call snippet tools directly                │\n│    ├── Can write code via execute_typescript         │\n│    └── Can register new snippets for future use       │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘","lang":"text"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"llm-calls","children":[{"type":"text","value":"LLM calls"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"There are "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"two"}]},{"type":"text","value":" LLM interactions per request when using the high-level API:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"loose":true,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Snippet selection"}]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"selectRelevantSnippets"},{"type":"text","value":") — A single chat call using the adapter you provide. It sends the last 5 conversation messages plus a catalog of snippet names/descriptions, and asks the model to return a JSON array of relevant snippet names. This should be a cheap/fast model (e.g., "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gpt-4o-mini"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"claude-haiku-4-5"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Main chat"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — The primary "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" call with your full model. This is where the LLM reasons, calls tools, writes code, and registers snippets."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The selection call is lightweight — it only sees snippet metadata (names, descriptions, usage hints), not full code. If there are no snippets in storage or no messages, it short-circuits and skips the LLM call entirely."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"high-level-api-codemodewithsnippets","children":[{"type":"text","value":"High-Level API: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"codeModeWithSnippets()"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"installation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"usage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Usage"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, maxIterations, toServerSentEventsStream } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { createNodeIsolateDriver } from '@tanstack/ai-isolate-node'\nimport { codeModeWithSnippets } from '@tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets'\nimport { createFileSnippetStorage } from '@tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets/storage'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { myTool1, myTool2 } from './tools'\n\nconst messages = [{ role: 'user' as const, content: 'Hello' }]\nconst storage = createFileSnippetStorage({ directory: './.snippets' })\nconst driver = createNodeIsolateDriver()\n\nconst { toolsRegistry, systemPrompt, selectedSnippets } = await codeModeWithSnippets({\n  config: {\n    driver,\n    tools: [myTool1, myTool2],\n    timeout: 60_000,\n    memoryLimit: 128,\n  },\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5-mini'),  // cheap model for snippet selection\n  snippets: {\n    storage,\n    maxSnippetsInContext: 5,\n  },\n  messages,  // current conversation\n})\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),  // strong model for reasoning\n  tools: toolsRegistry.getTools(),\n  messages,\n  systemPrompts: ['You are a helpful assistant.', systemPrompt],\n  agentLoopStrategy: maxIterations(15),\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"codeModeWithSnippets"},{"type":"text","value":" returns:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Property"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolsRegistry"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ToolRegistry"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mutable registry containing all tools. Pass to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tools: toolsRegistry.getTools()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"systemPrompt"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Combined Code Mode + snippet library documentation."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"selectedSnippets"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Array<Snippet>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Snippets the selection model chose for this conversation."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"what-goes-into-the-registry","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What goes into the registry"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The registry is populated with:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"execute_typescript"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — The Code Mode sandbox tool. Inside the sandbox, snippets are also available as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"snippet_*"},{"type":"text","value":" functions (loaded dynamically at execution time)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"search_snippets"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — Search the snippet library by query. Returns matching snippet metadata."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"get_snippet"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — Retrieve full details (including code) for a specific snippet."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"register_snippet"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — Save working code as a new snippet. Newly registered snippets are immediately added to the registry as callable tools."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"One tool per selected snippet"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — Each selected snippet becomes a direct tool (prefixed with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[SNIPPET]"},{"type":"text","value":" in its description) that the LLM can call without going through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"execute_typescript"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"manual-api","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Manual API"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you want full control — for example, loading all snippets instead of using LLM-based selection — use the lower-level functions directly. This is the approach used in the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ts-code-mode-web"},{"type":"text","value":" example."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, maxIterations } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { createCodeMode } from '@tanstack/ai-code-mode'\nimport { createNodeIsolateDriver } from '@tanstack/ai-isolate-node'\nimport {\n  createAlwaysTrustedStrategy,\n  createSnippetManagementTools,\n  createSnippetsSystemPrompt,\n  snippetsToTools,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets'\nimport { createFileSnippetStorage } from '@tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets/storage'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { myTool1, myTool2, BASE_PROMPT } from './tools'\n\nconst messages = [{ role: 'user' as const, content: 'Hello' }]\nconst trustStrategy = createAlwaysTrustedStrategy()\nconst storage = createFileSnippetStorage({\n  directory: './.snippets',\n  trustStrategy,\n})\nconst driver = createNodeIsolateDriver()\n\n// 1. Create Code Mode tool + prompt\nconst { tool: codeModeTool, systemPrompt: codeModePrompt } =\n  createCodeMode({\n    driver,\n    tools: [myTool1, myTool2],\n    timeout: 60_000,\n    memoryLimit: 128,\n  })\n\n// 2. Load all snippets and convert to tools\nconst allSnippets = await storage.loadAll()\nconst snippetIndex = await storage.loadIndex()\n\nconst snippetTools = allSnippets.length > 0\n  ? snippetsToTools({\n      snippets: allSnippets,\n      driver,\n      tools: [myTool1, myTool2],\n      storage,\n      timeout: 60_000,\n      memoryLimit: 128,\n    })\n  : []\n\n// 3. Create management tools\nconst managementTools = createSnippetManagementTools({\n  storage,\n  trustStrategy,\n})\n\n// 4. Generate snippet library prompt\nconst snippetsPrompt = createSnippetsSystemPrompt({\n  selectedSnippets: allSnippets,\n  totalSnippetCount: snippetIndex.length,\n  snippetsAsTools: true,\n})\n\n// 5. Assemble and call chat()\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n  tools: [codeModeTool, ...managementTools, ...snippetTools],\n  messages,\n  systemPrompts: [BASE_PROMPT, codeModePrompt, snippetsPrompt],\n  agentLoopStrategy: maxIterations(15),\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This approach skips the selection LLM call entirely — you load whichever snippets you want and pass them in directly."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"snippet-storage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Snippet Storage"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Snippets are persisted through the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SnippetStorage"},{"type":"text","value":" interface. Two implementations are provided:"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"file-storage-production","children":[{"type":"text","value":"File storage (production)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createFileSnippetStorage"},{"type":"text","value":" is Node-only — it imports "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"node:fs"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"node:path"},{"type":"text","value":" — so\nit lives behind the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/storage"},{"type":"text","value":" subpath rather than the package root. This keeps\nthe root export safe to bundle for Cloudflare Workers and browser builds; only\nreach for the subpath in a Node runtime."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createFileSnippetStorage } from '@tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets/storage'\nimport { createDefaultTrustStrategy } from '@tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets'\n\nconst trustStrategy = createDefaultTrustStrategy()\nconst storage = createFileSnippetStorage({\n  directory: './.snippets',\n  trustStrategy,  // optional, defaults to createDefaultTrustStrategy()\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a directory structure:"}]},{"type":"code","value":".snippets/\n  _index.json              # Lightweight catalog for fast loading\n  fetch_github_stats/\n    meta.json              # Description, schemas, hints, stats\n    code.ts                # TypeScript source\n  compare_npm_packages/\n    meta.json\n    code.ts","lang":"text"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"memory-storage-testing-edge-runtimes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Memory storage (testing & edge runtimes)"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createMemorySnippetStorage } from '@tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets'\n\nconst storage = createMemorySnippetStorage()","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keeps everything in memory — no "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"node:fs"},{"type":"text","value":" dependency, so it is re-exported from\nthe package root and is safe to use in Workers and browsers. Useful for tests,\ndemos, and edge deployments. (It is also available from the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/storage"},{"type":"text","value":" subpath.)"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"storage-interface","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Storage interface"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Both implementations satisfy this interface:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Method"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loadIndex()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Load lightweight metadata for all snippets (no code)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loadAll()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Load all snippets with full details including code"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"get(name)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Get a single snippet by name"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"save(snippet)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create or update a snippet"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"delete(name)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Remove a snippet"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"search(query, options?)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Search snippets by text query"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"updateStats(name, success)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Record an execution result for trust tracking"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"trust-strategies","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Trust Strategies"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Snippets start untrusted and earn trust through successful executions. The trust level is metadata only — it does not currently gate execution. Four built-in strategies are available:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  createDefaultTrustStrategy,\n  createAlwaysTrustedStrategy,\n  createRelaxedTrustStrategy,\n  createCustomTrustStrategy,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets'","lang":"typescript","meta":"group=code-mode-with-snippets"},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Strategy"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Initial level"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provisional"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Trusted"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"untrusted"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"10+ runs, ≥90% success"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"100+ runs, ≥95% success"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Relaxed"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"untrusted"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3+ runs, ≥80% success"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"10+ runs, ≥90% success"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Always trusted"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"trusted"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"—"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"—"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configurable"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configurable"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configurable"}]}]]},{"type":"code","value":"const strategy = createCustomTrustStrategy({\n  initialLevel: 'untrusted',\n  provisionalThreshold: { executions: 5, successRate: 0.85 },\n  trustedThreshold: { executions: 50, successRate: 0.95 },\n})","lang":"typescript","meta":"group=code-mode-with-snippets"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"snippet-lifecycle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Snippet Lifecycle"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"registration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Registration"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When the LLM produces useful code via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"execute_typescript"},{"type":"text","value":", the system prompt instructs it to call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"register_snippet"},{"type":"text","value":" with:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":" — snake_case identifier (becomes the tool name)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"description"},{"type":"text","value":" — what the snippet does"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code"},{"type":"text","value":" — TypeScript source that receives an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"input"},{"type":"text","value":" variable"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"inputSchema"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"outputSchema"},{"type":"text","value":" — JSON Schema strings"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"usageHints"},{"type":"text","value":" — when to use this snippet"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dependsOn"},{"type":"text","value":" — other snippets this one calls"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The snippet is saved to storage and (if a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ToolRegistry"},{"type":"text","value":" was provided) immediately added as a callable tool in the current session."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"execution","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Execution"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When a snippet tool is called, the system:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wraps the snippet code with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"const input = <serialized input>;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Strips TypeScript syntax to plain JavaScript"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a fresh sandbox context with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"external_*"},{"type":"text","value":" bindings"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Executes the code and returns the result"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Updates execution stats (success/failure count) asynchronously"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"selection-high-level-api-only","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Selection (high-level API only)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On each new request, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"selectRelevantSnippets"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Takes the last 5 conversation messages as context"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Builds a catalog from the snippet index (name + description + first usage hint)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Asks the adapter to return a JSON array of relevant snippet names (max "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxSnippetsInContext"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Loads full snippet data for the selected names"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If parsing fails or the model returns invalid JSON, it falls back to an empty selection — the request proceeds without pre-loaded snippets, but the LLM can still search and use snippets via the management tools."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"snippets-as-tools-vs-sandbox-bindings","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Snippets as Tools vs. Sandbox Bindings"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"snippetsAsTools"},{"type":"text","value":" option (default: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":") controls how snippets are exposed:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mode"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How the LLM calls a snippet"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pros"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cons"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"As tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Direct tool call: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"snippet_name({ ... })"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Simpler for the LLM, shows in tool-call UI, proper input validation"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"One tool per snippet in the tool list"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"As bindings"}]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Inside "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"execute_typescript"},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"await snippet_fetch_data({ ... })"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Snippets composable in code, fewer top-level tools"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"LLM must write code to use them"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"snippetsAsTools"},{"type":"text","value":" is enabled, the system prompt documents each snippet with its schema, usage hints, and example calls. When disabled, snippets appear as typed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"snippet_*"},{"type":"text","value":" functions in the sandbox type stubs."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"custom-events","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom Events"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Snippet execution emits events through the TanStack AI event system:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Event"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Payload"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code_mode:snippet_call"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Snippet tool invoked"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ snippet, input, timestamp }"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code_mode:snippet_result"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Snippet completed successfully"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ snippet, result, duration, timestamp }"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code_mode:snippet_error"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Snippet execution failed"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ snippet, error, duration, timestamp }"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"snippet:registered"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"New snippet saved via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"register_snippet"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ id, name, description, timestamp }"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To render these events in your React app alongside Code Mode execution events, see "},{"type":"link","href":"./client-integration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Showing Code Mode in the UI"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"tips","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tips"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use a cheap model for selection."}]},{"type":"text","value":" The selection call only needs to match snippet names to conversation context — "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gpt-4o-mini"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"claude-haiku-4-5"},{"type":"text","value":" work well."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Start without snippets."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Get Code Mode working first, then add "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets"},{"type":"text","value":" once you have tools that produce reusable patterns."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Monitor the snippet count."}]},{"type":"text","value":" As the library grows, consider increasing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxSnippetsInContext"},{"type":"text","value":" or switching to the manual API where you control which snippets load."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Newly registered snippets are available on the next message,"}]},{"type":"text","value":" not in the current turn's tool list (unless using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ToolRegistry"},{"type":"text","value":" with the high-level API, which adds them immediately)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Snippets can call other snippets."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Inside the sandbox, both "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"external_*"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"snippet_*"},{"type":"text","value":" functions are available. Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dependsOn"},{"type":"text","value":" when registering to document these relationships."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"next-steps","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next Steps"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./code-mode","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Code Mode"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — Core Code Mode setup and API reference"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./client-integration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Showing Code Mode in the UI"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — Display execution progress in your React app"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./code-mode-isolates","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Isolate Drivers"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — Compare sandbox runtimes"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"id":"how-it-works","text":"How It Works","level":2},{"id":"llm-calls","text":"LLM calls","level":3},{"id":"high-level-api-codemodewithsnippets","text":"High-Level API: codeModeWithSnippets()","level":2},{"id":"installation","text":"Installation","level":3},{"id":"usage","text":"Usage","level":3},{"id":"what-goes-into-the-registry","text":"What goes into the registry","level":3},{"id":"manual-api","text":"Manual API","level":2},{"id":"snippet-storage","text":"Snippet Storage","level":2},{"id":"file-storage-production","text":"File storage (production)","level":3},{"id":"memory-storage-testing-edge-runtimes","text":"Memory storage (testing & edge runtimes)","level":3},{"id":"storage-interface","text":"Storage interface","level":3},{"id":"trust-strategies","text":"Trust Strategies","level":2},{"id":"snippet-lifecycle","text":"Snippet Lifecycle","level":2},{"id":"registration","text":"Registration","level":3},{"id":"execution","text":"Execution","level":3},{"id":"selection-high-level-api-only","text":"Selection (high-level API only)","level":3},{"id":"snippets-as-tools-vs-sandbox-bindings","text":"Snippets as Tools vs. Sandbox Bindings","level":2},{"id":"custom-events","text":"Custom Events","level":2},{"id":"tips","text":"Tips","level":2},{"id":"next-steps","text":"Next Steps","level":2}]},"frameworks":["react","vue","solid","svelte","preact","angular","vanilla","octane"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nSnippets extend [Code Mode](./code-mode.md) with a persistent library of reusable TypeScript snippets. When the LLM writes a useful piece of code — say, a function that fetches and ranks NPM packages — it can save that code as a _snippet_. On future requests, relevant snippets are loaded from storage and made available as first-class tools the LLM can call without re-writing the logic.\n\n> **Different from agent-authoring skills.** The snippets on this page are _runtime_ snippets the chat LLM saves and reuses. If you're looking to teach your coding assistant (Claude Code, Cursor, etc.) how TanStack AI itself works, see [Agent Skills (TanStack Intent)](../getting-started/agent-skills).\n\n## Overview\n\nThe snippets system has two integration paths:\n\n| Approach | Entry point | Snippet selection | Best for |\n|----------|-------------|----------------|----------|\n| **High-level** | `codeModeWithSnippets()` | Automatic (LLM-based) | New projects, turnkey setup |\n| **Manual** | Individual functions (`snippetsToTools`, `createSnippetManagementTools`, etc.) | You decide which snippets to load | Full control, existing setups |\n\nBoth paths share the same storage, trust, and execution primitives — they differ only in how snippets are selected and assembled.\n\n## How It Works\n\nA request with snippets enabled goes through these stages:\n\n```text\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ 1. Load snippet index (metadata only, no code)        │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 2. Select relevant snippets (LLM call — fast model)   │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 3. Build tool registry                              │\n│    ├── execute_typescript (Code Mode sandbox)        │\n│    ├── search_snippets / get_snippet / register_snippet   │\n│    └── snippet tools (one per selected snippet)         │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 4. Generate system prompt                           │\n│    ├── Code Mode type stubs                         │\n│    └── Snippet library documentation                  │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 5. Main chat() call (strong model)                  │\n│    ├── Can call snippet tools directly                │\n│    ├── Can write code via execute_typescript         │\n│    └── Can register new snippets for future use       │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### LLM calls\n\nThere are **two** LLM interactions per request when using the high-level API:\n\n1. **Snippet selection** (`selectRelevantSnippets`) — A single chat call using the adapter you provide. It sends the last 5 conversation messages plus a catalog of snippet names/descriptions, and asks the model to return a JSON array of relevant snippet names. This should be a cheap/fast model (e.g., `gpt-4o-mini`, `claude-haiku-4-5`).\n\n2. **Main chat** — The primary `chat()` call with your full model. This is where the LLM reasons, calls tools, writes code, and registers snippets.\n\nThe selection call is lightweight — it only sees snippet metadata (names, descriptions, usage hints), not full code. If there are no snippets in storage or no messages, it short-circuits and skips the LLM call entirely.\n\n## High-Level API: `codeModeWithSnippets()`\n\n### Installation\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets\nvue: @tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets\npreact: @tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets\nangular: @tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets\noctane: @tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n### Usage\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, maxIterations, toServerSentEventsStream } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { createNodeIsolateDriver } from '@tanstack/ai-isolate-node'\nimport { codeModeWithSnippets } from '@tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets'\nimport { createFileSnippetStorage } from '@tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets/storage'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { myTool1, myTool2 } from './tools'\n\nconst messages = [{ role: 'user' as const, content: 'Hello' }]\nconst storage = createFileSnippetStorage({ directory: './.snippets' })\nconst driver = createNodeIsolateDriver()\n\nconst { toolsRegistry, systemPrompt, selectedSnippets } = await codeModeWithSnippets({\n  config: {\n    driver,\n    tools: [myTool1, myTool2],\n    timeout: 60_000,\n    memoryLimit: 128,\n  },\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5-mini'),  // cheap model for snippet selection\n  snippets: {\n    storage,\n    maxSnippetsInContext: 5,\n  },\n  messages,  // current conversation\n})\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),  // strong model for reasoning\n  tools: toolsRegistry.getTools(),\n  messages,\n  systemPrompts: ['You are a helpful assistant.', systemPrompt],\n  agentLoopStrategy: maxIterations(15),\n})\n```\n\n`codeModeWithSnippets` returns:\n\n| Property | Type | Description |\n|----------|------|-------------|\n| `toolsRegistry` | `ToolRegistry` | Mutable registry containing all tools. Pass to `chat()` via `tools: toolsRegistry.getTools()`. |\n| `systemPrompt` | `string` | Combined Code Mode + snippet library documentation. |\n| `selectedSnippets` | `Array<Snippet>` | Snippets the selection model chose for this conversation. |\n\n### What goes into the registry\n\nThe registry is populated with:\n\n- **`execute_typescript`** — The Code Mode sandbox tool. Inside the sandbox, snippets are also available as `snippet_*` functions (loaded dynamically at execution time).\n- **`search_snippets`** — Search the snippet library by query. Returns matching snippet metadata.\n- **`get_snippet`** — Retrieve full details (including code) for a specific snippet.\n- **`register_snippet`** — Save working code as a new snippet. Newly registered snippets are immediately added to the registry as callable tools.\n- **One tool per selected snippet** — Each selected snippet becomes a direct tool (prefixed with `[SNIPPET]` in its description) that the LLM can call without going through `execute_typescript`.\n\n## Manual API\n\nIf you want full control — for example, loading all snippets instead of using LLM-based selection — use the lower-level functions directly. This is the approach used in the `ts-code-mode-web` example.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, maxIterations } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { createCodeMode } from '@tanstack/ai-code-mode'\nimport { createNodeIsolateDriver } from '@tanstack/ai-isolate-node'\nimport {\n  createAlwaysTrustedStrategy,\n  createSnippetManagementTools,\n  createSnippetsSystemPrompt,\n  snippetsToTools,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets'\nimport { createFileSnippetStorage } from '@tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets/storage'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { myTool1, myTool2, BASE_PROMPT } from './tools'\n\nconst messages = [{ role: 'user' as const, content: 'Hello' }]\nconst trustStrategy = createAlwaysTrustedStrategy()\nconst storage = createFileSnippetStorage({\n  directory: './.snippets',\n  trustStrategy,\n})\nconst driver = createNodeIsolateDriver()\n\n// 1. Create Code Mode tool + prompt\nconst { tool: codeModeTool, systemPrompt: codeModePrompt } =\n  createCodeMode({\n    driver,\n    tools: [myTool1, myTool2],\n    timeout: 60_000,\n    memoryLimit: 128,\n  })\n\n// 2. Load all snippets and convert to tools\nconst allSnippets = await storage.loadAll()\nconst snippetIndex = await storage.loadIndex()\n\nconst snippetTools = allSnippets.length > 0\n  ? snippetsToTools({\n      snippets: allSnippets,\n      driver,\n      tools: [myTool1, myTool2],\n      storage,\n      timeout: 60_000,\n      memoryLimit: 128,\n    })\n  : []\n\n// 3. Create management tools\nconst managementTools = createSnippetManagementTools({\n  storage,\n  trustStrategy,\n})\n\n// 4. Generate snippet library prompt\nconst snippetsPrompt = createSnippetsSystemPrompt({\n  selectedSnippets: allSnippets,\n  totalSnippetCount: snippetIndex.length,\n  snippetsAsTools: true,\n})\n\n// 5. Assemble and call chat()\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n  tools: [codeModeTool, ...managementTools, ...snippetTools],\n  messages,\n  systemPrompts: [BASE_PROMPT, codeModePrompt, snippetsPrompt],\n  agentLoopStrategy: maxIterations(15),\n})\n```\n\nThis approach skips the selection LLM call entirely — you load whichever snippets you want and pass them in directly.\n\n## Snippet Storage\n\nSnippets are persisted through the `SnippetStorage` interface. Two implementations are provided:\n\n### File storage (production)\n\n`createFileSnippetStorage` is Node-only — it imports `node:fs` / `node:path` — so\nit lives behind the `/storage` subpath rather than the package root. This keeps\nthe root export safe to bundle for Cloudflare Workers and browser builds; only\nreach for the subpath in a Node runtime.\n\n```typescript\nimport { createFileSnippetStorage } from '@tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets/storage'\nimport { createDefaultTrustStrategy } from '@tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets'\n\nconst trustStrategy = createDefaultTrustStrategy()\nconst storage = createFileSnippetStorage({\n  directory: './.snippets',\n  trustStrategy,  // optional, defaults to createDefaultTrustStrategy()\n})\n```\n\nCreates a directory structure:\n\n```text\n.snippets/\n  _index.json              # Lightweight catalog for fast loading\n  fetch_github_stats/\n    meta.json              # Description, schemas, hints, stats\n    code.ts                # TypeScript source\n  compare_npm_packages/\n    meta.json\n    code.ts\n```\n\n### Memory storage (testing & edge runtimes)\n\n```typescript\nimport { createMemorySnippetStorage } from '@tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets'\n\nconst storage = createMemorySnippetStorage()\n```\n\nKeeps everything in memory — no `node:fs` dependency, so it is re-exported from\nthe package root and is safe to use in Workers and browsers. Useful for tests,\ndemos, and edge deployments. (It is also available from the `/storage` subpath.)\n\n### Storage interface\n\nBoth implementations satisfy this interface:\n\n| Method | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| `loadIndex()` | Load lightweight metadata for all snippets (no code) |\n| `loadAll()` | Load all snippets with full details including code |\n| `get(name)` | Get a single snippet by name |\n| `save(snippet)` | Create or update a snippet |\n| `delete(name)` | Remove a snippet |\n| `search(query, options?)` | Search snippets by text query |\n| `updateStats(name, success)` | Record an execution result for trust tracking |\n\n## Trust Strategies\n\nSnippets start untrusted and earn trust through successful executions. The trust level is metadata only — it does not currently gate execution. Four built-in strategies are available:\n\n```typescript group=code-mode-with-snippets\nimport {\n  createDefaultTrustStrategy,\n  createAlwaysTrustedStrategy,\n  createRelaxedTrustStrategy,\n  createCustomTrustStrategy,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets'\n```\n\n| Strategy | Initial level | Provisional | Trusted |\n|----------|--------------|-------------|---------|\n| **Default** | `untrusted` | 10+ runs, ≥90% success | 100+ runs, ≥95% success |\n| **Relaxed** | `untrusted` | 3+ runs, ≥80% success | 10+ runs, ≥90% success |\n| **Always trusted** | `trusted` | — | — |\n| **Custom** | Configurable | Configurable | Configurable |\n\n```typescript group=code-mode-with-snippets\nconst strategy = createCustomTrustStrategy({\n  initialLevel: 'untrusted',\n  provisionalThreshold: { executions: 5, successRate: 0.85 },\n  trustedThreshold: { executions: 50, successRate: 0.95 },\n})\n```\n\n## Snippet Lifecycle\n\n### Registration\n\nWhen the LLM produces useful code via `execute_typescript`, the system prompt instructs it to call `register_snippet` with:\n\n- `name` — snake_case identifier (becomes the tool name)\n- `description` — what the snippet does\n- `code` — TypeScript source that receives an `input` variable\n- `inputSchema` / `outputSchema` — JSON Schema strings\n- `usageHints` — when to use this snippet\n- `dependsOn` — other snippets this one calls\n\nThe snippet is saved to storage and (if a `ToolRegistry` was provided) immediately added as a callable tool in the current session.\n\n### Execution\n\nWhen a snippet tool is called, the system:\n\n1. Wraps the snippet code with `const input = <serialized input>;`\n2. Strips TypeScript syntax to plain JavaScript\n3. Creates a fresh sandbox context with `external_*` bindings\n4. Executes the code and returns the result\n5. Updates execution stats (success/failure count) asynchronously\n\n### Selection (high-level API only)\n\nOn each new request, `selectRelevantSnippets`:\n\n1. Takes the last 5 conversation messages as context\n2. Builds a catalog from the snippet index (name + description + first usage hint)\n3. Asks the adapter to return a JSON array of relevant snippet names (max `maxSnippetsInContext`)\n4. Loads full snippet data for the selected names\n\nIf parsing fails or the model returns invalid JSON, it falls back to an empty selection — the request proceeds without pre-loaded snippets, but the LLM can still search and use snippets via the management tools.\n\n## Snippets as Tools vs. Sandbox Bindings\n\nThe `snippetsAsTools` option (default: `true`) controls how snippets are exposed:\n\n| Mode | How the LLM calls a snippet | Pros | Cons |\n|------|--------------------------|------|------|\n| **As tools** (`true`) | Direct tool call: `snippet_name({ ... })` | Simpler for the LLM, shows in tool-call UI, proper input validation | One tool per snippet in the tool list |\n| **As bindings** (`false`) | Inside `execute_typescript`: `await snippet_fetch_data({ ... })` | Snippets composable in code, fewer top-level tools | LLM must write code to use them |\n\nWhen `snippetsAsTools` is enabled, the system prompt documents each snippet with its schema, usage hints, and example calls. When disabled, snippets appear as typed `snippet_*` functions in the sandbox type stubs.\n\n## Custom Events\n\nSnippet execution emits events through the TanStack AI event system:\n\n| Event | When | Payload |\n|-------|------|---------|\n| `code_mode:snippet_call` | Snippet tool invoked | `{ snippet, input, timestamp }` |\n| `code_mode:snippet_result` | Snippet completed successfully | `{ snippet, result, duration, timestamp }` |\n| `code_mode:snippet_error` | Snippet execution failed | `{ snippet, error, duration, timestamp }` |\n| `snippet:registered` | New snippet saved via `register_snippet` | `{ id, name, description, timestamp }` |\n\nTo render these events in your React app alongside Code Mode execution events, see [Showing Code Mode in the UI](./client-integration).\n\n## Tips\n\n- **Use a cheap model for selection.** The selection call only needs to match snippet names to conversation context — `gpt-4o-mini` or `claude-haiku-4-5` work well.\n- **Start without snippets.** Get Code Mode working first, then add `@tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets` once you have tools that produce reusable patterns.\n- **Monitor the snippet count.** As the library grows, consider increasing `maxSnippetsInContext` or switching to the manual API where you control which snippets load.\n- **Newly registered snippets are available on the next message,** not in the current turn's tool list (unless using `ToolRegistry` with the high-level API, which adds them immediately).\n- **Snippets can call other snippets.** Inside the sandbox, both `external_*` and `snippet_*` functions are available. Set `dependsOn` when registering to document these relationships.\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [Code Mode](./code-mode) — Core Code Mode setup and API reference\n- [Showing Code Mode in the UI](./client-integration) — Display execution progress in your React app\n- [Isolate Drivers](./code-mode-isolates) — Compare sandbox runtimes\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Code Mode with Snippets\nid: code-mode-with-snippets\norder: 3\ndescription: \"Teach Code Mode to save and reuse working code as named snippets backed by persistent storage — faster follow-up requests and composable agent memory.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - code mode\n  - snippets\n  - snippet library\n  - register_snippet\n  - reusable snippets\n  - agent memory\n  - snippet storage\n---\n\nSnippets extend [Code Mode](./code-mode.md) with a persistent library of reusable TypeScript snippets. When the LLM writes a useful piece of code — say, a function that fetches and ranks NPM packages — it can save that code as a _snippet_. On future requests, relevant snippets are loaded from storage and made available as first-class tools the LLM can call without re-writing the logic.\n\n> **Different from agent-authoring skills.** The snippets on this page are _runtime_ snippets the chat LLM saves and reuses. If you're looking to teach your coding assistant (Claude Code, Cursor, etc.) how TanStack AI itself works, see [Agent Skills (TanStack Intent)](../getting-started/agent-skills).\n\n## Overview\n\nThe snippets system has two integration paths:\n\n| Approach | Entry point | Snippet selection | Best for |\n|----------|-------------|----------------|----------|\n| **High-level** | `codeModeWithSnippets()` | Automatic (LLM-based) | New projects, turnkey setup |\n| **Manual** | Individual functions (`snippetsToTools`, `createSnippetManagementTools`, etc.) | You decide which snippets to load | Full control, existing setups |\n\nBoth paths share the same storage, trust, and execution primitives — they differ only in how snippets are selected and assembled.\n\n## How It Works\n\nA request with snippets enabled goes through these stages:\n\n```text\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ 1. Load snippet index (metadata only, no code)        │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 2. Select relevant snippets (LLM call — fast model)   │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 3. Build tool registry                              │\n│    ├── execute_typescript (Code Mode sandbox)        │\n│    ├── search_snippets / get_snippet / register_snippet   │\n│    └── snippet tools (one per selected snippet)         │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 4. Generate system prompt                           │\n│    ├── Code Mode type stubs                         │\n│    └── Snippet library documentation                  │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 5. Main chat() call (strong model)                  │\n│    ├── Can call snippet tools directly                │\n│    ├── Can write code via execute_typescript         │\n│    └── Can register new snippets for future use       │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### LLM calls\n\nThere are **two** LLM interactions per request when using the high-level API:\n\n1. **Snippet selection** (`selectRelevantSnippets`) — A single chat call using the adapter you provide. It sends the last 5 conversation messages plus a catalog of snippet names/descriptions, and asks the model to return a JSON array of relevant snippet names. This should be a cheap/fast model (e.g., `gpt-4o-mini`, `claude-haiku-4-5`).\n\n2. **Main chat** — The primary `chat()` call with your full model. This is where the LLM reasons, calls tools, writes code, and registers snippets.\n\nThe selection call is lightweight — it only sees snippet metadata (names, descriptions, usage hints), not full code. If there are no snippets in storage or no messages, it short-circuits and skips the LLM call entirely.\n\n## High-Level API: `codeModeWithSnippets()`\n\n### Installation\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets\nvue: @tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets\npreact: @tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets\nangular: @tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets\noctane: @tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n### Usage\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, maxIterations, toServerSentEventsStream } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { createNodeIsolateDriver } from '@tanstack/ai-isolate-node'\nimport { codeModeWithSnippets } from '@tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets'\nimport { createFileSnippetStorage } from '@tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets/storage'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { myTool1, myTool2 } from './tools'\n\nconst messages = [{ role: 'user' as const, content: 'Hello' }]\nconst storage = createFileSnippetStorage({ directory: './.snippets' })\nconst driver = createNodeIsolateDriver()\n\nconst { toolsRegistry, systemPrompt, selectedSnippets } = await codeModeWithSnippets({\n  config: {\n    driver,\n    tools: [myTool1, myTool2],\n    timeout: 60_000,\n    memoryLimit: 128,\n  },\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5-mini'),  // cheap model for snippet selection\n  snippets: {\n    storage,\n    maxSnippetsInContext: 5,\n  },\n  messages,  // current conversation\n})\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),  // strong model for reasoning\n  tools: toolsRegistry.getTools(),\n  messages,\n  systemPrompts: ['You are a helpful assistant.', systemPrompt],\n  agentLoopStrategy: maxIterations(15),\n})\n```\n\n`codeModeWithSnippets` returns:\n\n| Property | Type | Description |\n|----------|------|-------------|\n| `toolsRegistry` | `ToolRegistry` | Mutable registry containing all tools. Pass to `chat()` via `tools: toolsRegistry.getTools()`. |\n| `systemPrompt` | `string` | Combined Code Mode + snippet library documentation. |\n| `selectedSnippets` | `Array<Snippet>` | Snippets the selection model chose for this conversation. |\n\n### What goes into the registry\n\nThe registry is populated with:\n\n- **`execute_typescript`** — The Code Mode sandbox tool. Inside the sandbox, snippets are also available as `snippet_*` functions (loaded dynamically at execution time).\n- **`search_snippets`** — Search the snippet library by query. Returns matching snippet metadata.\n- **`get_snippet`** — Retrieve full details (including code) for a specific snippet.\n- **`register_snippet`** — Save working code as a new snippet. Newly registered snippets are immediately added to the registry as callable tools.\n- **One tool per selected snippet** — Each selected snippet becomes a direct tool (prefixed with `[SNIPPET]` in its description) that the LLM can call without going through `execute_typescript`.\n\n## Manual API\n\nIf you want full control — for example, loading all snippets instead of using LLM-based selection — use the lower-level functions directly. This is the approach used in the `ts-code-mode-web` example.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, maxIterations } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { createCodeMode } from '@tanstack/ai-code-mode'\nimport { createNodeIsolateDriver } from '@tanstack/ai-isolate-node'\nimport {\n  createAlwaysTrustedStrategy,\n  createSnippetManagementTools,\n  createSnippetsSystemPrompt,\n  snippetsToTools,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets'\nimport { createFileSnippetStorage } from '@tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets/storage'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { myTool1, myTool2, BASE_PROMPT } from './tools'\n\nconst messages = [{ role: 'user' as const, content: 'Hello' }]\nconst trustStrategy = createAlwaysTrustedStrategy()\nconst storage = createFileSnippetStorage({\n  directory: './.snippets',\n  trustStrategy,\n})\nconst driver = createNodeIsolateDriver()\n\n// 1. Create Code Mode tool + prompt\nconst { tool: codeModeTool, systemPrompt: codeModePrompt } =\n  createCodeMode({\n    driver,\n    tools: [myTool1, myTool2],\n    timeout: 60_000,\n    memoryLimit: 128,\n  })\n\n// 2. Load all snippets and convert to tools\nconst allSnippets = await storage.loadAll()\nconst snippetIndex = await storage.loadIndex()\n\nconst snippetTools = allSnippets.length > 0\n  ? snippetsToTools({\n      snippets: allSnippets,\n      driver,\n      tools: [myTool1, myTool2],\n      storage,\n      timeout: 60_000,\n      memoryLimit: 128,\n    })\n  : []\n\n// 3. Create management tools\nconst managementTools = createSnippetManagementTools({\n  storage,\n  trustStrategy,\n})\n\n// 4. Generate snippet library prompt\nconst snippetsPrompt = createSnippetsSystemPrompt({\n  selectedSnippets: allSnippets,\n  totalSnippetCount: snippetIndex.length,\n  snippetsAsTools: true,\n})\n\n// 5. Assemble and call chat()\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n  tools: [codeModeTool, ...managementTools, ...snippetTools],\n  messages,\n  systemPrompts: [BASE_PROMPT, codeModePrompt, snippetsPrompt],\n  agentLoopStrategy: maxIterations(15),\n})\n```\n\nThis approach skips the selection LLM call entirely — you load whichever snippets you want and pass them in directly.\n\n## Snippet Storage\n\nSnippets are persisted through the `SnippetStorage` interface. Two implementations are provided:\n\n### File storage (production)\n\n`createFileSnippetStorage` is Node-only — it imports `node:fs` / `node:path` — so\nit lives behind the `/storage` subpath rather than the package root. This keeps\nthe root export safe to bundle for Cloudflare Workers and browser builds; only\nreach for the subpath in a Node runtime.\n\n```typescript\nimport { createFileSnippetStorage } from '@tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets/storage'\nimport { createDefaultTrustStrategy } from '@tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets'\n\nconst trustStrategy = createDefaultTrustStrategy()\nconst storage = createFileSnippetStorage({\n  directory: './.snippets',\n  trustStrategy,  // optional, defaults to createDefaultTrustStrategy()\n})\n```\n\nCreates a directory structure:\n\n```text\n.snippets/\n  _index.json              # Lightweight catalog for fast loading\n  fetch_github_stats/\n    meta.json              # Description, schemas, hints, stats\n    code.ts                # TypeScript source\n  compare_npm_packages/\n    meta.json\n    code.ts\n```\n\n### Memory storage (testing & edge runtimes)\n\n```typescript\nimport { createMemorySnippetStorage } from '@tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets'\n\nconst storage = createMemorySnippetStorage()\n```\n\nKeeps everything in memory — no `node:fs` dependency, so it is re-exported from\nthe package root and is safe to use in Workers and browsers. Useful for tests,\ndemos, and edge deployments. (It is also available from the `/storage` subpath.)\n\n### Storage interface\n\nBoth implementations satisfy this interface:\n\n| Method | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| `loadIndex()` | Load lightweight metadata for all snippets (no code) |\n| `loadAll()` | Load all snippets with full details including code |\n| `get(name)` | Get a single snippet by name |\n| `save(snippet)` | Create or update a snippet |\n| `delete(name)` | Remove a snippet |\n| `search(query, options?)` | Search snippets by text query |\n| `updateStats(name, success)` | Record an execution result for trust tracking |\n\n## Trust Strategies\n\nSnippets start untrusted and earn trust through successful executions. The trust level is metadata only — it does not currently gate execution. Four built-in strategies are available:\n\n```typescript group=code-mode-with-snippets\nimport {\n  createDefaultTrustStrategy,\n  createAlwaysTrustedStrategy,\n  createRelaxedTrustStrategy,\n  createCustomTrustStrategy,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets'\n```\n\n| Strategy | Initial level | Provisional | Trusted |\n|----------|--------------|-------------|---------|\n| **Default** | `untrusted` | 10+ runs, ≥90% success | 100+ runs, ≥95% success |\n| **Relaxed** | `untrusted` | 3+ runs, ≥80% success | 10+ runs, ≥90% success |\n| **Always trusted** | `trusted` | — | — |\n| **Custom** | Configurable | Configurable | Configurable |\n\n```typescript group=code-mode-with-snippets\nconst strategy = createCustomTrustStrategy({\n  initialLevel: 'untrusted',\n  provisionalThreshold: { executions: 5, successRate: 0.85 },\n  trustedThreshold: { executions: 50, successRate: 0.95 },\n})\n```\n\n## Snippet Lifecycle\n\n### Registration\n\nWhen the LLM produces useful code via `execute_typescript`, the system prompt instructs it to call `register_snippet` with:\n\n- `name` — snake_case identifier (becomes the tool name)\n- `description` — what the snippet does\n- `code` — TypeScript source that receives an `input` variable\n- `inputSchema` / `outputSchema` — JSON Schema strings\n- `usageHints` — when to use this snippet\n- `dependsOn` — other snippets this one calls\n\nThe snippet is saved to storage and (if a `ToolRegistry` was provided) immediately added as a callable tool in the current session.\n\n### Execution\n\nWhen a snippet tool is called, the system:\n\n1. Wraps the snippet code with `const input = <serialized input>;`\n2. Strips TypeScript syntax to plain JavaScript\n3. Creates a fresh sandbox context with `external_*` bindings\n4. Executes the code and returns the result\n5. Updates execution stats (success/failure count) asynchronously\n\n### Selection (high-level API only)\n\nOn each new request, `selectRelevantSnippets`:\n\n1. Takes the last 5 conversation messages as context\n2. Builds a catalog from the snippet index (name + description + first usage hint)\n3. Asks the adapter to return a JSON array of relevant snippet names (max `maxSnippetsInContext`)\n4. Loads full snippet data for the selected names\n\nIf parsing fails or the model returns invalid JSON, it falls back to an empty selection — the request proceeds without pre-loaded snippets, but the LLM can still search and use snippets via the management tools.\n\n## Snippets as Tools vs. Sandbox Bindings\n\nThe `snippetsAsTools` option (default: `true`) controls how snippets are exposed:\n\n| Mode | How the LLM calls a snippet | Pros | Cons |\n|------|--------------------------|------|------|\n| **As tools** (`true`) | Direct tool call: `snippet_name({ ... })` | Simpler for the LLM, shows in tool-call UI, proper input validation | One tool per snippet in the tool list |\n| **As bindings** (`false`) | Inside `execute_typescript`: `await snippet_fetch_data({ ... })` | Snippets composable in code, fewer top-level tools | LLM must write code to use them |\n\nWhen `snippetsAsTools` is enabled, the system prompt documents each snippet with its schema, usage hints, and example calls. When disabled, snippets appear as typed `snippet_*` functions in the sandbox type stubs.\n\n## Custom Events\n\nSnippet execution emits events through the TanStack AI event system:\n\n| Event | When | Payload |\n|-------|------|---------|\n| `code_mode:snippet_call` | Snippet tool invoked | `{ snippet, input, timestamp }` |\n| `code_mode:snippet_result` | Snippet completed successfully | `{ snippet, result, duration, timestamp }` |\n| `code_mode:snippet_error` | Snippet execution failed | `{ snippet, error, duration, timestamp }` |\n| `snippet:registered` | New snippet saved via `register_snippet` | `{ id, name, description, timestamp }` |\n\nTo render these events in your React app alongside Code Mode execution events, see [Showing Code Mode in the UI](./client-integration).\n\n## Tips\n\n- **Use a cheap model for selection.** The selection call only needs to match snippet names to conversation context — `gpt-4o-mini` or `claude-haiku-4-5` work well.\n- **Start without snippets.** Get Code Mode working first, then add `@tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets` once you have tools that produce reusable patterns.\n- **Monitor the snippet count.** As the library grows, consider increasing `maxSnippetsInContext` or switching to the manual API where you control which snippets load.\n- **Newly registered snippets are available on the next message,** not in the current turn's tool list (unless using `ToolRegistry` with the high-level API, which adds them immediately).\n- **Snippets can call other snippets.** Inside the sandbox, both `external_*` and `snippet_*` functions are available. Set `dependsOn` when registering to document these relationships.\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [Code Mode](./code-mode) — Core Code Mode setup and API reference\n- [Showing Code Mode in the UI](./client-integration) — Display execution progress in your React app\n- [Isolate Drivers](./code-mode-isolates) — Compare sandbox runtimes\n"}
